course: dictionary
lesson: 13939
title: A hard word with a hurtful history
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A leper is a person who has leprosy, an illness of the skin and nerves. In Bible times, lepers had to live apart from other people and call out «Unclean!» to warn them. Jesus touched and healed lepers.
explain: «Jesus healed ten lepers, and only one came back to say thank you.» The story teaches gratitude, which means being thankful. Touching the leper shows compassion, which means caring about people that others push away.
explain: Leper has a second meaning too: a person that others avoid or reject. «Ben was treated like a leper when everyone left him out of the game.» The clue is left out: Ben was avoided by the others, so treated like a leper means he was shunned.
explain: Today many people say «a person with leprosy» instead of leper, because leper can be hurtful. When you write or talk about people, choose kind and clear words.
fact: A leper is a person who has leprosy, an illness of the skin and nerves.
fact: «Leper» can also mean a person that others avoid or reject.
fact: Phrases you may meet are «treated like a leper», «the ten lepers» and «leper colony».
fact: Today people prefer «a person with leprosy», because «leper» can be hurtful.
fact: Gratitude means being thankful, and compassion means caring about someone's suffering.
exercise: «Jesus healed ten lepers in the Bible story.» What does leper mean? | A person who sings in a choir | A person who lives on a farm | A person who is very old | *A person who has leprosy, an illness of the skin and nerves
exercise: «Ben was treated like a leper when everyone left him out.» What does leper mean here? | A kind teacher | A famous singer | *A person that others avoid or reject
exercise: Only one of the ten lepers came back to say thank you. Which word means being thankful? | Leprosy | Compassion | Colony | *Gratitude
test: Why do many people now say «a person with leprosy» instead of leper? | *Because leper can be hurtful | Because leprosy means happy | Because lepers never lived apart | Because leper is a longer word
test: In the Bible story, what did lepers have to call out to warn people? | Help me! | Thank you! | *Unclean! | Hello!
exam: Which word means caring about people that others push away? | Gratitude | Colony | Leprosy | *Compassion
